# trieScanVariable writes the terminating NUL one byte past a 100-byte
# buffer when a variable name is exactly 100 bytes long. See FINDINGS.md,
# E9. Run under the ASan build to see the report; the normal build
# silently overwrites one byte of stack.

set name [string repeat x 100]
Assert! the thing is here
sleep 0.2
QuerySimple! 0 the thing is /$name/
Exit! 0
